{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WL2uEwdaJD6QDoYLN7LPEs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Configuration reference\n2\t\n3\tTwo files and two environment variables.\n4\t\n5\t## Worker config — `~/.config/hivedispatch/config.yaml`\n6\t\n7\tWritten by `hivedispatch init`; every command takes `-config PATH` to use another file.\n8\t\n9\t| Key | Default | Meaning |\n10\t|---|---|---|\n11\t| `tracker` | `jira` | `jira` or `github` (GitHub Issues: labels carry state, a hidden body marker carries the claim) |\n12\t| `agent_id` | *(required)* | Name of this worker; written to tickets it claims |\n13\t| `workroot` | `~/.local/share/hivedispatch` | Clones, worktrees, and state live under here |\n14\t| `poll_interval` | `60s` | Time between polls |\n15\t| `poll_jitter` | `10s` | Random extra wait per poll, so several workers do not poll in lockstep |\n16\t| `heartbeat_interval` | `60s` | How often a running worker refreshes its claim |\n17\t| `claim_timeout` | `2h` | A claim not refreshed for this long is abandoned; another worker may take it. Must exceed `heartbeat_interval` and any realistic run |\n18\t| `run_timeout` | `45m` | Wall-clock limit for one executor run |\n19\t| `step_budget` | `200` | Tool calls per executor run before it is stopped |\n20\t| `max_attempts` | `3` | Failed attempts before a ticket goes to Needs Human |\n21\t| `retention_days` | `30` | Raw run logs and finished run records older than this are pruned at startup; `-1` never prunes |\n22\t| `executor` | `claude` | `claude` or `fake` (no agent; useful for trying the pipeline) |\n23\t| `claude.binary` | `claude` | The Claude Code CLI to run |\n24\t| `claude.model` | *(CLI default)* | Model for the executor when the repo policy sets none |\n25\t| `triage.kind` | `claude` | `claude` (read-only model triage) or `passthrough` (dispatch everything) |\n26\t| `triage.step_budget` | `40` | Tool calls the triager may make |\n27\t| `triage.timeout` | `5m` | Wall-clock limit for triage |\n28\t| `triage.model` | *(CLI default)* | Model for triage |\n29\t| `state_store` | `branch` | `branch` keeps run state on `hive/state` in each repo; `local` keeps it under `workroot/state` |\n30\t| `jira.base_url` | *(required)* | `https://<site>.atlassian.net` |\n31\t| `jira.email` | *(required)* | Atlassian account the token belongs to |\n32\t| `jira.jql` | *(required)* | Trigger query: which tickets the worker may take |\n33\t| `jira.fields.agent_id` | *(by name)* | `customfield_NNNNN` of \"HiveDispatch Agent\"; leave empty to resolve by name |\n34\t| `jira.fields.claimed_at` | *(by name)* | `customfield_NNNNN` of \"HiveDispatch Claimed At\" |\n35\t| `jira.statuses.ready` … `needs_human` | `Ready`, `In Progress`, `Needs Info`, `In Review`, `Needs Human` | Workflow status names in your project |\n36\t| `github.api_url` | `https://api.github.com` | Change for GitHub Enterprise |\n37\t| `repos[].name` | *(required)* | `owner/repo` |\n38\t| `repos[].url` | *(required)* | Clone URL your git credentials can push to |\n39\t| `repos[].default_branch` | `main` | Base for ticket branches and PRs |\n40\t| `repos[].project` | *(required)* | Ticket key prefix. Jira: the project key (`SCRUM` for `SCRUM-4`). GitHub Issues: any short upper-case tag; issue #12 becomes `TAG-12`. `jira_project` is accepted as an alias |\n41\t| `github.labels.ready` … `needs_human` | `hive:ready`, `hive:in-progress`, `hive:needs-info`, `hive:in-review`, `hive:needs-human` | State labels when `tracker: github` |\n42\t| `run_windows.timezone` | local | IANA zone for the windows |\n43\t| `run_windows.windows[]` | *(none = always)* | `{days: [mon, …], start: \"22:00\", end: \"06:00\"}`; `start` after `end` spans midnight. Windows gate the start of new work only |\n44\t\n45\t## Repo policy — `.hivedispatch.yaml` at the repository root\n46\t\n47\tRead from the ticket's worktree, so it is versioned with the code and can differ per branch.\n48\t\n49\t| Key | Default | Meaning |\n50\t|---|---|---|\n51\t| `executor.model` | worker `claude.model` | Model for runs in this repo |\n52\t| `executor.permission_mode` | `dontAsk` | Claude Code permission mode: `acceptEdits`, `auto`, `bypassPermissions`, `manual`, `dontAsk`, `plan`. `dontAsk` fails closed |\n53\t| `executor.tools` | `[default]` | Built-in tool set, or a list to restrict |\n54\t| `executor.allowed_tools` | *(none)* | Pre-approved patterns for `dontAsk`, e.g. `Edit`, `\"Bash(go test:*)\"` |\n55\t| `executor.max_budget_usd` | *(none)* | Per-run spend cap (API-billed accounts) |\n56\t| `executor.path` | *(none)* | Directories prepended to the agent's `PATH` (`~` and `$VAR` expand), e.g. `[\"~/go/bin\"]` so `golangci-lint` resolves |\n57\t| `guidance` | *(none)* | Text appended to every prompt for this repo: conventions, required checks, where decisions are recorded |\n58\t\n59\t## Environment\n60\t\n61\t| Variable | Required | Meaning |\n62\t|---|---|---|\n63\t| `HIVE_JIRA_TOKEN` | yes | Atlassian API token for `jira.email` |\n64\t| `HIVE_GITHUB_TOKEN` | with `tracker: github` | Token for opening PRs and, with `tracker: github`, for reading and writing issues. Classic or fine-grained, interchangeably — see the token table in `docs/setup.md` §5 for which permissions each needs; a user-owned Projects board requires a classic token. If unset, `gh auth token` and the git credential helper are tried; with none and Jira, branches are pushed and the ticket asks a human to open the PR |\n65\t\n66\t## Commands\n67\t\n68\t| Command | What it does |\n69\t|---|---|\n70\t| `init` | Write the starter worker config (never overwrites a non-empty file) |\n71\t| `init -jira` | Create the two claim fields in Jira |\n72\t| `init -github` | Create the state labels in each GitHub repository |\n73\t| `check [-live]` | Validate the config; with `-live`, verify the tracker (Jira: credentials, fields, editability, statuses, projects, trigger query; GitHub: token, repos, labels) |\n74\t| `run [-once]` | Preflight, then poll and dispatch (once, or until Ctrl-C: first drains, second interrupts) |\n75\t| `once KEY` | Handle one ticket by key, ignoring the trigger query and run windows |\n76\t| `status [-json]` | List run records from the state branch(es) |\n77\t| `version` | Print the version |\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7de223-5e43-4120-ae08-3d4a6a3cb28c","uuid":"d170c47f-8a8c-4069-acb0-349a5d68b830","timestamp":"2026-09-20T07:08:03.330Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/thomas/.local/share/hivedispatch/repos/thomasmeadows__HiveDispatch/GITHUB-8/docs/config.md","content":"# Configuration reference\n\nTwo files and two environment variables.\n\n## Worker config — `~/.config/hivedispatch/config.yaml`\n\nWritten by `hivedispatch init`; every command takes `-config PATH` to use another file.\n\n| Key | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tracker` | `jira` | `jira` or `github` (GitHub Issues: labels carry state, a hidden body marker carries the claim) |\n| `agent_id` | *(required)* | Name of this worker; written to tickets it claims |\n| `workroot` | `~/.local/share/hivedispatch` | Clones, worktrees, and state live under here |\n| `poll_interval` | `60s` | Time between polls |\n| `poll_jitter` | `10s` | Random extra wait per poll, so several workers do not poll in lockstep |\n| `heartbeat_interval` | `60s` | How often a running worker refreshes its claim |\n| `claim_timeout` | `2h` | A claim not refreshed for this long is abandoned; another worker may take it. Must exceed `heartbeat_interval` and any realistic run |\n| `run_timeout` | `45m` | Wall-clock limit for one executor run |\n| `step_budget` | `200` | Tool calls per executor run before it is stopped |\n| `max_attempts` | `3` | Failed attempts before a ticket goes to Needs Human |\n| `retention_days` | `30` | Raw run logs and finished run records older than this are pruned at startup; `-1` never prunes |\n| `executor` | `claude` | `claude` or `fake` (no agent; useful for trying the pipeline) |\n| `claude.binary` | `claude` | The Claude Code CLI to run |\n| `claude.model` | *(CLI default)* | Model for the executor when the repo policy sets none |\n| `triage.kind` | `claude` | `claude` (read-only model triage) or `passthrough` (dispatch everything) |\n| `triage.step_budget` | `40` | Tool calls the triager may make |\n| `triage.timeout` | `5m` | Wall-clock limit for triage |\n| `triage.model` | *(CLI default)* | Model for triage |\n| `state_store` | `branch` | `branch` keeps run state on `hive/state` in each repo; `local` keeps it under `workroot/state` |\n| `jira.base_url` | *(required)* | `https://<site>.atlassian.net` |\n| `jira.email` | *(required)* | Atlassian account the token belongs to |\n| `jira.jql` | *(required)* | Trigger query: which tickets the worker may take |\n| `jira.fields.agent_id` | *(by name)* | `customfield_NNNNN` of \"HiveDispatch Agent\"; leave empty to resolve by name |\n| `jira.fields.claimed_at` | *(by name)* | `customfield_NNNNN` of \"HiveDispatch Claimed At\" |\n| `jira.statuses.ready` … `needs_human` | `Ready`, `In Progress`, `Needs Info`, `In Review`, `Needs Human` | Workflow status names in your project |\n| `github.api_url` | `https://api.github.com` | Change for GitHub Enterprise |\n| `repos[].name` | *(required)* | `owner/repo` |\n| `repos[].url` | *(required)* | Clone URL your git credentials can push to |\n| `repos[].default_branch` | `main` | Base for ticket branches and PRs |\n| `repos[].project` | *(required)* | Ticket key prefix. Jira: the project key (`SCRUM` for `SCRUM-4`). GitHub Issues: any short upper-case tag; issue #12 becomes `TAG-12`. `jira_project` is accepted as an alias |\n| `github.labels.ready` … `needs_human` | `hive:ready`, `hive:in-progress`, `hive:needs-info`, `hive:in-review`, `hive:needs-human` | State labels when `tracker: github` |\n| `run_windows.timezone` | local | IANA zone for the windows |\n| `run_windows.windows[]` | *(none = always)* | `{days: [mon, …], start: \"22:00\", end: \"06:00\"}`; `start` after `end` spans midnight. Windows gate the start of new work only |\n\n## Repo policy — `.hivedispatch.yaml` at the repository root\n\nRead from the ticket's worktree, so it is versioned with the code and can differ per branch.\n\n| Key | Default | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `executor.model` | worker `claude.model` | Model for runs in this repo |\n| `executor.permission_mode` | `dontAsk` | Claude Code permission mode: `acceptEdits`, `auto`, `bypassPermissions`, `manual`, `dontAsk`, `plan`. `dontAsk` fails closed |\n| `executor.tools` | `[default]` | Built-in tool set, or a list to restrict |\n| `executor.allowed_tools` | *(none)* | Pre-approved patterns for `dontAsk`, e.g. `Edit`, `\"Bash(go test:*)\"` |\n| `executor.max_budget_usd` | *(none)* | Per-run spend cap (API-billed accounts) |\n| `executor.path` | *(none)* | Directories prepended to the agent's `PATH` (`~` and `$VAR` expand), e.g. `[\"~/go/bin\"]` so `golangci-lint` resolves |\n| `guidance` | *(none)* | Text appended to every prompt for this repo: conventions, required checks, where decisions are recorded |\n\n## Environment\n\n| Variable | Required | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `HIVE_JIRA_TOKEN` | yes | Atlassian API token for `jira.email` |\n| `HIVE_GITHUB_TOKEN` | with `tracker: github` | Token for opening PRs and, with `tracker: github`, for reading and writing issues. Classic or fine-grained, interchangeably — see the token table in `docs/setup.md` §5 for which permissions each needs; a user-owned Projects board requires a classic token. If unset, `gh auth token` and the git credential helper are tried; with none and Jira, branches are pushed and the ticket asks a human to open the PR |\n\n## Commands\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `init` | Write the starter worker config (never overwrites a non-empty file) |\n| `init -jira` | Create the two claim fields in Jira |\n| `init -github` | Create the state labels in each GitHub repository |\n| `check [-live]` | Validate the config; with `-live`, verify the tracker (Jira: credentials, fields, editability, statuses, projects, trigger query; GitHub: token, repos, labels) |\n| `run [-once]` | Preflight, then poll and dispatch (once, or until Ctrl-C: first drains, second interrupts) |\n| `once KEY` | Handle one ticket by key, ignoring the trigger query and run windows |\n| `status [-json]` | List run records from the state branch(es) |\n| `version` | Print the version |\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
