{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfEGvM97cuChtqKwvnSH5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0115qVNFgXf56HeKymAXFrb1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/thomas/.local/share/hivedispatch/repos/thomasmeadows__HiveDispatch/GITHUB-8/docs/setup.md","offset":185,"limit":45},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2794,"cache_read_input_tokens":113589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2794},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7de223-5e43-4120-ae08-3d4a6a3cb28c","uuid":"d799fb0e-6b5f-4824-b7fb-b2407f2f9b2d","timestamp":"2026-09-20T07:11:57.464Z","request_id":"req_011CfEGvLXtZ9idfmxCgp5SF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0115qVNFgXf56HeKymAXFrb1":{"file_path":"/home/thomas/.local/share/hivedispatch/repos/thomasmeadows__HiveDispatch/GITHUB-8/docs/setup.md","offset":185,"limit":45}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0115qVNFgXf56HeKymAXFrb1","type":"tool_result","content":"185\tOn each transition the worker adds the issue to the board if it is not there yet and sets the field; labels remain the queue and the source of truth, so a board that cannot be reached is logged and never blocks a run.\n186\t\n187\tChoose a `project` that no Jira project on the same worker uses. Ticket keys are the identity for branches, run records and worktrees; `SCRUM-5` from Jira and issue #5 in a repo with `project: SCRUM` would share all three.\n188\t\n189\t## 9. Claude Code\n190\t\n191\tThe worker shells out to the `claude` CLI. Log in once as the user that runs the worker (`claude` then `/login`) — headless runs reuse the stored credentials. Do not set `--bare` anywhere; it skips credential loading.\n192\t\n193\tPer-repo policy lives in `.hivedispatch.yaml` at the repository root:\n194\t\n195\t```yaml\n196\texecutor:\n197\t  model: sonnet                 # optional; default is the CLI's default\n198\t  permission_mode: dontAsk      # acceptEdits | auto | bypassPermissions | manual | dontAsk | plan\n199\t  tools: [default]              # built-in tool set; use a list to restrict\n200\t  allowed_tools:                # pre-approved patterns for dontAsk mode\n201\t    - Edit\n202\t    - \"Bash(go test:*)\"\n203\t  max_budget_usd: 5             # optional; API-billing accounts only\n204\tguidance: |\n205\t  Free text appended to every prompt for this repo.\n206\t```\n207\t\n208\t`dontAsk` fails closed: anything not in `allowed_tools` is denied and the agent must work around it or ask. `bypassPermissions` is for sandboxed runs only.\n209\t\n210\tAllowlist patterns match whole tokens by prefix, so `Bash(golangci-lint:*)` allows `golangci-lint run ./...` but not `/home/me/go/bin/golangci-lint run` — put tool directories on the agent's `PATH` with `executor.path` instead of allowing absolute paths.\n211\t\n212\tThe run log for each attempt is saved to the state branch under `logs/<KEY>/<timestamp>.log`.\n213\t\n214\t### Triage\n215\t\n216\tTriage runs the same CLI read-only (`--restricted`, Read/Grep/Glob, plan mode) in the ticket worktree with its own bounds:\n217\t\n218\t```yaml\n219\ttriage:\n220\t  kind: claude          # or passthrough: dispatch every ticket without a model call\n221\t  step_budget: 40       # tool calls\n222\t  timeout: 5m\n223\t  model: sonnet         # optional\n224\t```\n225\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7de223-5e43-4120-ae08-3d4a6a3cb28c","uuid":"d1613288-96ec-4ef5-8a36-f7f8769f130a","timestamp":"2026-09-20T07:11:57.468Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/thomas/.local/share/hivedispatch/repos/thomasmeadows__HiveDispatch/GITHUB-8/docs/setup.md","content":"On each transition the worker adds the issue to the board if it is not there yet and sets the field; labels remain the queue and the source of truth, so a board that cannot be reached is logged and never blocks a run.\n\nChoose a `project` that no Jira project on the same worker uses. Ticket keys are the identity for branches, run records and worktrees; `SCRUM-5` from Jira and issue #5 in a repo with `project: SCRUM` would share all three.\n\n## 9. Claude Code\n\nThe worker shells out to the `claude` CLI. Log in once as the user that runs the worker (`claude` then `/login`) — headless runs reuse the stored credentials. Do not set `--bare` anywhere; it skips credential loading.\n\nPer-repo policy lives in `.hivedispatch.yaml` at the repository root:\n\n```yaml\nexecutor:\n  model: sonnet                 # optional; default is the CLI's default\n  permission_mode: dontAsk      # acceptEdits | auto | bypassPermissions | manual | dontAsk | plan\n  tools: [default]              # built-in tool set; use a list to restrict\n  allowed_tools:                # pre-approved patterns for dontAsk mode\n    - Edit\n    - \"Bash(go test:*)\"\n  max_budget_usd: 5             # optional; API-billing accounts only\nguidance: |\n  Free text appended to every prompt for this repo.\n```\n\n`dontAsk` fails closed: anything not in `allowed_tools` is denied and the agent must work around it or ask. `bypassPermissions` is for sandboxed runs only.\n\nAllowlist patterns match whole tokens by prefix, so `Bash(golangci-lint:*)` allows `golangci-lint run ./...` but not `/home/me/go/bin/golangci-lint run` — put tool directories on the agent's `PATH` with `executor.path` instead of allowing absolute paths.\n\nThe run log for each attempt is saved to the state branch under `logs/<KEY>/<timestamp>.log`.\n\n### Triage\n\nTriage runs the same CLI read-only (`--restricted`, Read/Grep/Glob, plan mode) in the ticket worktree with its own bounds:\n\n```yaml\ntriage:\n  kind: claude          # or passthrough: dispatch every ticket without a model call\n  step_budget: 40       # tool calls\n  timeout: 5m\n  model: sonnet         # optional\n```\n","numLines":41,"startLine":185,"totalLines":225}}}
