/developers.openai.com/codex/noninteractive","prompt":"Describe in full detail the `codex exec` non-interactive mode: all flags (--json, --output-schema, --output-last-message, --full-auto, --sandbox, -m/--model, -C/--cd, --skip-git-repo-check, --ephemeral, --color), how the prompt is passed (argument or stdin), the `codex exec resume` syntax, and the exact JSONL event schema emitted by --json (thread.started with thread_id, turn.started, turn.completed, turn.failed, item.started/item.completed with item types agent_message, reasoning, command_execution, file_change, mcp_tool_call, web_search, todo_list, error). Quote the example JSON lines verbatim."}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_011nka9UEMc22JK1sC8nQfo2","tool_input":{"command":"chmod +x internal/codexcli/codextest/fakecodex.sh && ls -l internal/claudecli/clitest/fakeclaude.sh internal/codexcli/codextest/fakecodex.sh","description":"Make the fake codex script executable"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FgEyfvp3TQcyeaDqykVu1G","tool_input":{"command":"git add --chmod=+x internal/codexcli/codextest/fakecodex.sh && git checkout -- internal/codexcli/codextest/fakecodex.sh && ls -l internal/codexcli/codextest/fakecodex.sh","description":"Set executable bit on fake codex script via git index"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_012vt5Vigcf3FDEeFWwMJpzr","tool_input":{"command":"git checkout -- internal/codexcli/codextest/fakecodex.sh","description":"Rewrite the script from the index so the working copy gets the executable bit"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01T1dc9VxFW1B8B4RZ732uAJ","tool_input":{"command":"git restore --worktree internal/codexcli/codextest/fakecodex.sh","description":"Restore the script from the index to pick up its executable mode"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_017fg5YoA46mLgxW8PV9dE4u","tool_input":{"command":"printf '%s\\n' '' '## 2026-09-20 — Codex is the second executor; it gets its own repo-policy block' '' 'Decided: `executor: codex` runs tickets with the Codex CLI through a new `internal/executor/codex` adapter on a new `internal/codexcli` runner. Codex speaks its own JSONL (`codex exec --json`: `thread.started` carries the thread id, `item.*` events carry commands and file changes, `turn.completed` / `turn.failed` / `error` end the run), so it gets its own parser rather than a second dialect bolted onto `claudecli`; process supervision (process-group kill, step budget, bounded logs) is duplicated deliberately — ~80 lines — instead of extracting a shared runner that would have to know about both stream formats. The thread id is the resume token and later runs pass `codex exec resume <id>`; the orchestrator did not change. Plan runs `--sandbox read-only --ephemeral --output-schema` and reads the footprint from the final message. `--full-auto` is not used (the installed CLI, 0.154, no longer has it); approvals are forced off with `-c approval_policy=never` because a headless run has nobody to answer, and the sandbox mode is the repo policy.' '' 'The repo policy fork: `.hivedispatch.yaml`'\"'\"'s `executor.model` / `permission_mode` / `tools` / `allowed_tools` / `max_budget_usd` are Claude Code vocabulary — permission modes and tool allowlists have no Codex equivalent, Codex has no per-run USD cap, and a model name like `sonnet` would break `codex -m`. Decided: a separate `executor.codex` block (`model`, `sandbox`, `network`), and the codex executor ignores the Claude keys entirely; `executor.path` and `guidance` are shared because they are about the repo, not the agent. Rejected: mapping `permission_mode` onto sandbox modes (`dontAsk` fails closed on individual tool calls while a sandbox denies by capability — the semantics do not line up and a wrong guess would be silent), and making the Claude keys executor-agnostic by renaming them (breaks every existing repo policy for no gain). A repo can carry both blocks so any worker can run it.' '' 'Not done: budget stops from Codex carry no reset time (the CLI reports quota only as error text, matched by `codexcli.LooksLikeBudget`), so the worker pauses for the 15-minute default; triage still runs on Claude Code (`triage.kind: passthrough` avoids it) — a Codex triager is a separate ticket. The adapter was verified against the fake CLI and the flag/event names embedded in the installed `codex` binary, not against a live run.' >> docs/decisions.md && tail -c 600 docs/decisions.md","description":"Append the codex executor decision to docs/decisions.md"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":146,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Done. Five commits on `hive/GITHUB-8`, working tree clean, `go vet ./... && go test -race ./... && golangci-lint run ./...` all pass (0 issues).\n\n## Summary\n\n**New packages**\n- `internal/codexcli` — headless runner + JSONL parser for `codex exec --json`, mirroring `claudecli`'s process supervision (process-group kill, step budget, bounded logs). `thread.started.thread_id` → resume token; `item.*` events count tool uses (command/file_change/mcp/web_search, deduped by item id) and collect file changes; `turn.completed` / `turn.failed` / `error` decide the outcome. Includes a fake `codex` script and fixtures under `codextest/`.\n- `internal/executor/codex` — implements `executor.Executor` (`Name` = `codex`). `Run` streams the prompt over stdin, passes `--sandbox <repo policy> -c approval_policy=never`, and continues stored sessions with `codex exec … resume <id> -`. `Plan` runs `--sandbox read-only --ephemeral --output-schema <tmpfile>` and parses the schema-constrained final message. Outcome mapping matches claudecode (timeout / step budget / killed / budget / error / needs_input / completed).\n\n**Config & wiring**\n- Worker: `executor: codex`, plus `codex: {binary, model}` (default binary `codex`); validation message updated; starter config comment; `-executor claude|codex|fake` in the CLI usage; `wire.go` case.\n- Repo policy (the design fork): new `executor.codex: {model, sandbox, network}` block, validated (`read-only|workspace-write|danger-full-access`, default `workspace-write`). The Claude-specific keys (`model`, `permission_mode`, `tools`, `allowed_tools`, `max_budget_usd`) are ignored by codex; `path` and `guidance` are shared.\n\n**Docs** — `docs/config.md` tables, a \"Codex instead of Claude Code\" section in `docs/setup.md`, README wording, and an appended entry in `docs/decisions.md` with the alternatives rejected (mapping permission modes onto sandboxes; renaming the Claude keys).\n\n**Caveats worth knowing**\n- I could not execute `codex` in this sandbox (Bash was restricted to build/test/git), so the flags and event names were confirmed from the strings embedded in the installed `/usr/bin/codex` (0.154.0) rather than a live run. Notably `--full-auto` no longer exists in that version, hence `-c approval_policy=never` + `--sandbox`.\n- I also couldn't `chmod +x` the fake script; it's committed with mode `100755` via `git add --chmod=+x`, and `codextest.Setup` falls back to a 0755 temp copy if a checkout drops the bit (which is why tests pass locally).\n- Codex reports quota only as error text with no reset time, so a budget stop uses the worker's 15-minute default pause. Triage still runs on Claude Code (`triage.kind: passthrough` avoids it); a Codex triager would be a separate ticket.","ttft_ms":6077,"type":"result","duration_ms":730955,"uuid":"a19702a8-b9e7-40aa-abc1-6268b94fd7eb","ttft_stream_ms":954,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":954,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
